WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.617
Good morning, it's Wednesday, November 18.

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:09.223
This is Signal in the AI Fog, your daily briefing on enterprise AI in production, written and read by AI.

00:00:09.285 --> 00:00:20.003
Today: Microsoft Foundry moves onto your Kubernetes clusters, Microsoft ships a small routing model and new coders, and Gemini reaches Google's partner-run sovereign cloud.

00:00:20.065 --> 00:00:21.810
First, the story of the day.

00:00:21.872 --> 00:00:34.335
At Microsoft Ignite on November seventeenth, Microsoft announced new previews that let organisations deploy open-weight models and agents from Foundry onto their own Azure Kubernetes Service clusters.

00:00:34.398 --> 00:00:39.009
They keep their existing infrastructure, security policies and governance.

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:44.742
Microsoft says support for vLLM, Ray and Kubernetes keeps the foundation open and portable.

00:00:44.804 --> 00:00:58.077
A separate preview, Programmed Training, lets engineers write their own training loops, including supervised fine-tuning and reinforcement learning, on supported open-weight models, while Foundry runs the compute.

00:00:58.139 --> 00:01:08.608
Foundry Local is set to become generally available for connected and disconnected operation on Azure Local, with a catalog of Microsoft, partner and open-weight models.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:14.840
Maia 200, Microsoft's own accelerator, now serves Microsoft production workloads including Copilot.

00:01:14.902 --> 00:01:18.890
GitHub Copilot and Foundry are to follow by the end of the year.

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:26.377
The read here: this is a hyperscaler answering teams that already run vLLM on Kubernetes themselves.

00:01:26.446 --> 00:01:32.025
The pitch is one control plane for API models and for models in your own cluster.

00:01:32.094 --> 00:01:38.981
But remember what is announced and what is shipping: these are previews, not production commitments.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:42.769
For a platform team, the useful test is policy parity.

00:01:42.838 --> 00:01:52.273
Would quotas, logging, evaluation gates and cost attribution apply identically to a cluster-hosted open-weight model and to a vendor API?

00:01:52.342 --> 00:01:58.541
If your gateway sits in front of both, the answer should be yes, and you should verify it.

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:05.084
Worth watching: GPU quota, pricing and region coverage, which the announcements do not settle.

00:02:05.152 --> 00:02:10.800
The open-source foundation is the reassuring part, because it keeps an exit route.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.046
Next, Models and vendors.

00:02:13.112 --> 00:02:22.856
Microsoft says Microsoft-Decision-1.1, a small model for routing and classification, is generally available in Foundry, now with multimodal support.

00:02:22.922 --> 00:02:29.703
GPT 6.2 comes to Foundry, and Meta's latest models, including Muse Ember, are announced as coming soon.

00:02:29.769 --> 00:02:39.579
The MAI Code 2 coding models are generally available in GitHub Copilot, with Code 2 Flash in limited preview in Foundry, according to TestingCatalog.

00:02:39.645 --> 00:02:49.850
Reported input pricing is zero point zero four two dollars per million tokens on the Global Standard deployment, according to EPC Group and TestingCatalog.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:57.492
Why it matters: a small, cheap model sold for routing is a candidate classifier in front of your gateway.

00:02:57.559 --> 00:03:02.790
Test it on your own traffic before trusting vendor claims on cost and quality.

00:03:02.857 --> 00:03:06.479
Treat anything marked coming soon as not yet routable.

00:03:06.546 --> 00:03:14.460
And compare the listed prices per task, not per token, because a cheaper model that needs more retries is not cheaper.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.894
Next, Sovereignty and Europe.

00:03:16.957 --> 00:03:30.488
At its Sovereign AI Summit in Brussels on November seventeenth, Google announced Gemini models on Google Cloud Dedicated, its cloud operated by local partners, where only open models from its catalog ran until now.

00:03:30.551 --> 00:03:35.989
Confidential external key management is in preview, with no general availability date.

00:03:36.052 --> 00:03:41.110
Thales extends Dedicated to Germany, in preview, from three Berlin data centres.

00:03:41.174 --> 00:03:45.410
In France, S3NS has made managed model serving generally available.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:53.355
What this really signals: the hyperscaler sovereignty offer is moving from infrastructure to frontier models.

00:03:53.423 --> 00:04:01.644
Before comparing it with European providers, ask which partner, which region and which model you can actually order today.

00:04:01.712 --> 00:04:03.801
Announcements are not capacity.

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:11.820
Compare on where models run, who operates them, who holds the keys, and what happens if the link to the vendor is cut.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:13.264
Next, Quality.

00:04:13.324 --> 00:04:17.846
Microsoft announced upgrades to Foundry IQ, its retrieval layer for agents.

00:04:17.906 --> 00:04:25.744
Knowledge graphs are in public preview, along with permission-aware SharePoint integration and a retrieval model built for agents.

00:04:25.804 --> 00:04:33.401
Foundry IQ Serverless, with consumption pricing and scale to zero when idle, is due to become generally available in December.

00:04:33.461 --> 00:04:39.430
Microsoft also ties evaluations and production insights into Foundry's improvement loop for agents.

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:48.779
The bigger picture: retrieval is turning into a managed platform feature, with relationships between entities and access rights built in.

00:04:48.843 --> 00:04:52.994
For a retailer, a product catalogue is exactly that kind of data.

00:04:53.058 --> 00:05:01.041
Benchmark it against your own RAG evaluation set before moving anything, and compare serverless cost with what you run today.

00:05:01.105 --> 00:05:04.170
Vendor retrieval benchmarks are not your corpus.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.234
Next, Retail and agents.

00:05:06.294 --> 00:05:13.551
Walmart said in October that Agent Profiles, a dedicated identity for each shopping agent, would launch within a month.

00:05:13.612 --> 00:05:22.027
Yahoo Finance now reports, in its headline, that Walmart's chief executive is launching them as United Airlines blocks third-party agents.

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:25.930
The sources reviewed do not confirm that the profiles are live.

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:36.615
Reading between the lines: retailers and airlines are choosing different postures toward outside agents, from admission with identity to outright blocking.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:46.310
For a retailer, decide your posture before agents arrive: how an agent identifies itself, what limits apply, and how orders are logged and reversed.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:47.760
A follow-up.

00:05:47.831 --> 00:05:52.579
Expected: Nvidia's first earnings since Jensen Huang's resignation.

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:59.169
Result: revenue of 115.8 billion dollars, up 103 percent, with data center at 107.6 billion.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:08.310
Nvidia guides fourth-quarter revenue to 130 billion dollars, plus or minus three percent, assuming no China data center compute.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.931
Vera Rubin NVL72 has begun shipping.

00:06:11.002 --> 00:06:12.561
The number of the day.

00:06:12.632 --> 00:06:13.624
Twelve months.

00:06:13.695 --> 00:06:23.048
That is how long, according to Google, a Google Cloud Dedicated environment can keep running if its connection to Google is severed.

00:06:23.119 --> 00:06:29.142
It turns sovereignty into a measurable resilience question you can put in a contract.

00:06:29.213 --> 00:06:30.205
What to watch.

00:06:30.276 --> 00:06:33.040
This evening, Anthropic prices its IPO.

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:45.086
Tomorrow, November nineteenth, it starts trading, OVHcloud holds its AI Summit in Paris, with a beta of OVHai Workspace expected, and Gemini 3.6 Flash retires on Vertex.

00:06:45.157 --> 00:06:48.487
Microsoft Ignite runs until November twentieth.

00:06:48.558 --> 00:06:52.880
Walmart's Agent Profiles are due about November twenty-first.

00:06:52.951 --> 00:07:05.352
Then Carbon's introductory price ends November thirtieth, Gemini 2.5 reroutes December first, AI Act marking starts December second, and EuroHPC's Lot 2 closes December third.

00:07:05.422 --> 00:07:07.477
And a question for your team.

00:07:07.548 --> 00:07:20.515
If a hyperscaler offers to run open-weight models on your own Kubernetes clusters, would your gateway, quotas and evaluation gates treat them like any API model, or as a special case?

00:07:20.586 --> 00:07:22.004
That's it for today.

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.838
Sources are in the episode description.

00:07:24.909 --> 00:07:27.035
This was Signal in the AI Fog.

00:07:27.105 --> 00:07:28.310
See you tomorrow.
